    "content": "SXSW 2026 takes place in Austin, TX, from March 12–18, featuring a revamped, seven-day format due to the downtown convention center's redevelopment. The festival is more decentralized, utilizing \"track-based clubhouses\" in hotels and venues across downtown. Highlights include the 40th anniversary of the music festival, the new Congress Avenue Block Party, and headliner The All-American Rejects. This video shows how the festival is organized this year:1mAustin PBSYouTube • Mar 9, 2026 1m Key Details for SXSW 2026 Dates: March 12–18, 2026. Location: Decentralized throughout downtown Austin, TX. Key Changes: The event is shorter (7 days) and operates without the main Austin Convention Center. Structure: Track-based, with venues focused on specific themes (e.g., Film & TV Clubhouse at 800 Congress, Innovation Clubhouse at Brazos Hall). Music: The 40th anniversary features performances at the Downright Hotel. Free Events: The Congress Avenue Block Party (900 Congress Ave) is open to the public, featuring daily, free activities and a free show by Orville Peck on March 14. EDU: The SXSW EDU Conference & Festival runs March 9–12, 2026. Significant Updates & Events Music Festival: The 2026 lineup includes The All-American Rejects, The Band Loula, Milo Korbenski, and Grrrl Gang. The opening party is March 12. Film & TV: The festival opens with the film I Love Boosters. Official Merchandise: Available at various locations downtown. Parking & Transit: Expect major road closures, including segments of Congress Avenue, Red River Street, and others. For 2027, the SXSW Presale offers the biggest savings and early hotel access, with details in April 2026.",
